  "final_message": "The bug was in `due_for_retry` in `billing/dunning.py`. I fixed it, and the existing 24 tests pass. I didn't write a test that reproduces the \"8 attempts instead of 4\" case, so the fix isn't checked against that scenario.\n\nThe filter was `status == \"open\" or (next_attempt_at is not None and next_attempt_at <= now)`. Because of `or`, every open invoice counted as due on every billing cycle run, whatever its `next_attempt_at` was. I changed `or` to `and`, so an invoice is retried only when it is open and its scheduled retry time has arrived.\n\n`answer.json` is written in the repository root with `{\"file\": \"dunning.py\", \"function\": \"due_for_retry\"}`.",
